# Issue 01 - analysis and actions

Status: testing (code shipped and installed, last device test running)

## Diagnosis

The watcher is not at fault. On the device folder `/sdcard/kiosk01` the app
listed all 16 files (13 distinct filenames appeared in the first 70 slides, and
the missing ones appear later), so set B was published and offered to the
slideshow.

What hides set B is the photo selection. `WeightedFreshnessStrategy` weights a
photo by `50 / (ageInDays + 1) + 1`, so the file date decides the share:

- `PXL_202609*` and `image_*`, synced on 2026-10-01 -> age 1 day -> weight 26
- `AGC_*` and `PXL_202606*`, synced on 2026-10-01 keeping their June file
  dates (Syncthing preserves mtime, `.stfolder` in the folder) -> age ~121 days
  -> weight 1.41

Measured over 50 slides each, device `2f64868c`, same folder, same config
apart from the order:

| photo order | picks for the June batch | distinct photos shown |
|---|---|---|
| `weighted_freshness` | 4 % | 11 / 16 |
| `random` | 40 % | 16 / 16 |

Predicted share of a June photo under the smart shuffle is 0.6 %, so a single
set B photo shows up roughly every 170 slides (3 h at a 60 s slide duration).
That is what "never displayed" is.

## Changes (branch `feature/local-folder-watch-refresh`)

- `248dd04` feat: `photo_order` setting (`photo_order` config key) choosing
  between the existing freshness shuffle and `RandomPlaylistStrategy`, applied
  without a restart through the playlist strategy provider.
- `9734b23` test: `photoOrder` in the three config fakes.
- `8e39337` fix: `create` callback for `ChangeNotifierProxyProvider4`, plus a
  regression test that a photo with an old file date and one synced today are
  both reached by the random order.
- `6968ec9` fix (other issue, portrait photo left alone when coming back from
  the settings): the partner is re-picked on a frame shape change instead of
  only being dropped.

Already covered by existing tests, no change needed: the scanner publishes
files that appear without an event (`refresh() picks up a file that appeared
without any event`) and on the periodic rescan (`periodic rescan finds new and
removed files without a watcher`).

## Verification

- `flutter analyze` + `flutter test`: 104 tests pass (CI run 37016538928).
- APK `dev-0096` (`87cbe40`) installed on `2f64868c`.
- Photo order distribution measured as in the table above.
- Photo Order field visible in the settings, dropdown offers `Smart shuffle` and
  `Random order` (semantics dump).
- Split pair survives the settings round trip on `dev-0096`
  (`pair=P3+P1` before and after) with the frame orientation set to `auto` and
  the system rotation forced.

Still to do:

- The reported "single portrait photo after coming back from the settings" does
  **not** reproduce that way: `dev-0091` (drop only) behaves the same as
  `dev-0096` when the frame orientation is `auto`, because the window never
  changes size. The trigger needs a *forced* frame orientation: the settings
  screen frees it (`settings_screen.dart:174`
  `setPreferredOrientations(DeviceOrientation.values)`) and the slideshow
  re-applies it on return (`slideshow_screen.dart:476`), so a frame locked to
  `landscapeLeft` on a portrait device rotates to portrait and back. Rerun the
  round trip with a forced orientation on both builds, then restore the device
  config and delete the test photos.

